# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Why this file exists: `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows checkout writes CRLF
# into the working tree while git stores LF. Prettier reads the working tree, so
# `npm run lint` failed with hundreds of `Delete ␍` errors on files nobody had
# touched -- 158 of 282 tracked files. That is worse than noise: it buried
# whether a real change was clean, so the only way to review one's own lint
# output was to grep the CRLF errors away and hope nothing real was hiding
# behind them.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf per-repo, so this holds regardless of anyone's
# global git config or which machine they clone onto.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must not be touched by any of the above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
